    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Deborah Klein Lopez was elected to the Agoura Hills City Council in 2018. She worked in financial analysis and project management before serving as a staffer in the California State Senate and Assembly. She managed a weekly winter homeless shelter for over 16 years. Following the Woolsey Fire, she supported a Climate Action and Adaptation Plan. She chaired the Clean Power Alliance board from 2024 to 2026. Her campaign says she will focus on wildfire preparedness, expanding access to healthcare, creating jobs, and increasing the supply of attainable housing. She also volunteered as campaign manager for a $27 million parcel tax measure for the Las Virgenes Unified School District.",
